# ── Output of generate_pages.py ──
# Every page, redirect stub and discovery file the generator writes — ~300 of
# them, plus sitemap.xml, robots.txt and llms.txt — and nothing else, so the
# folder itself can be the rule. deploy.yml builds it in CI and copies it over
# the checkout before uploading; committing it would churn 300 files on every
# content edit and bury the one-line change that actually happened.
#
# It used to be written into the source tree, and this file then needed twenty
# patterns to name the generated files without swallowing the source beside
# them (a blanket `information/` once hid three committed-looking images that
# were never pushed). One folder of pure output needs one line.
/_generated/

# ── Full-size sources for the derivatives ──
# Every one of these is the original a committed web copy was encoded from —
# keep them locally so a derivative can be regenerated, but they are megabytes
# each and no page ever requests them. See "The size budget" in CLAUDE.md.
*_full.jpg
*_full.png
*_full.webp
*_full.gif
img/Intro.mp4
news/*/featured_poster.png

# ── Local noise ──
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
*.DS_Store

analytics/